# TERMINAL STATE — levels/L6-polysemantic.lvl
#
# L6 · "Polysemantic" — REBUILT to the 2026-09-23 (real-world) owner-approved spatial
# redesign (the spatial redesign §3 L6) + the final puzzle graph
# (the puzzle-graph redesign §L6).
#
# CAMPAIGN SLOT: manifest #6 · movement P2 "THE CALIBRATION WING" · load ▆ (rise)
# IDENTITY: an octagonal planetarium ten cells high. Three stars hang in a
# black sky, their light falls in wires to your hands, and a lattice arcs
# across the northern sky, looking back.
#
# ── MECHANIC (pure data — one node, two REQUIRED door targets, plus a rival
#    shortcut) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   vega   (IN=1) ─┐
#   altair (IN=1) ─┼─►  triangle (T=3)  ─┬─►  out_named   (T=1)  ─┐
#   deneb  (IN=1) ─┘                     └─►  out_watched (T=1)  ─┴─► door
#                  └──►  void_det (T=1, hidden) ──► out_named   (the shortcut)
#
# `triangle` is the polysemantic unit: its pool mixes the SHAPE field
# (TRIANGLE / PATTERN / CONSTELLATION) and the GAZE field (RESOLVE / WATCHER),
# and the door requires BOTH readings — `target_parts = out_named
# out_watched`. `re_puzzle::check_win` needs EVERY door target, so there is no
# path that keeps one meaning and drops the other.
#
# 2026-09-23 (real-world) GRAPH FIX (the puzzle-graph redesign §L6,
# owner-approved). The shipped graph's decoy (`deneb->void_det`) led nowhere
# the door cared about — "all-but-the-decoy" is the whole solve. `void_det`
# now feeds a NEW pipe, `void_det->out_named`: two cheap wires
# (`deneb->void_det` + `void_det->out_named`) light `out_named` and its
# `named_block` emit for 2 units instead of the honest route's 3
# (`vega->triangle` + `altair->triangle`/`deneb->triangle` + `triangle->out_named`),
# but under `power_budget = 5` that shortcut always leaves exactly one unit
# short of also lighting `out_watched` — "the pretty half" M.S.'s note warns
# against. The honest solve (5 toggles, all three stars + both triangle
# outputs) is still the only way to open the door.
#
# SOLUTION (5 toggles): vega->triangle, altair->triangle, deneb->triangle,
#   triangle->out_named, triangle->out_watched — all ON. Leave deneb->void_det
#   and void_det->out_named OFF: next to the name there is an emptiness, and
#   wiring yourself to it is BETWEEN-STARS, HOLLOW, gone — and it is also, now,
#   a trap that spends the unit the honest half needs.
#
# READOUT (WORD_STORY §RESULT, canon): VEGA + ALTAIR + DENEB -> ASTERISM -> NAMED
# NAME SHARD 6: `named` — to be named is to become reachable.
#
# ── THE WATCHING LATTICE (PROGRESSION §2 L6(e), STORY_BIBLE §7) ───────────────
# The whole north arc, PLUS the two northern chamfer faces, is a
# `[wall_decal] surface = matrix` region skinned with the shipped `watcher`
# catalog material: a world-fixed grid that reads as a face and has been
# looking back the whole time. It is visible from the FIRST frame now — the
# spawn faces it directly across the room (the spatial redesign §3 L6 Walk) — not
# from behind the door as before.
#
# ── AUTHORING NOTE: the second output's pool ──────────────────────────────────
# WORD_STORY §2 gives L6 ONE output row (`NAMED MAP CHART SKY-FRAME RECOGNIZED
# OUTPUT`) and the polysemantic fan-out needs TWO. The second pool is taken
# verbatim from the shipped `levels/06.lvl` `out_grid` node (`GRID LATTICE MESH
# COLD-READ MAPPED`) — the canon polysemantic file — rather than invented here.
# CONTENT_PACK's guardrail applies: the pool in the `.lvl` is the source of truth.
#
# ── TOKEN DISCIPLINE (W1 allowlist) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# No `{token}` appears in this file. FORM 07 carries none.
#
# ── SPACE (the spatial redesign §3 L6) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# 21x21x10 octagon (four 45° corner chamfers, 5 cells each), z=1..8 open,
# ceiling z=9. Star nodes hang at z=4; each wire drops straight down to z=2 —
# "the light falling" — before running to `triangle`. `[room] ambient = solid`
# (D1 fix): the dark-violet `body` wall material now actually paints the
# perimeter and the chamfer faces instead of the inert trace-pattern binding.
# No lamps: the sky is lit by starlight (`[atmosphere] key_dir = 0,0,1`) alone.
#
# Verify:
#   cargo run -q -p re_game -- --dump levels/L6-polysemantic.lvl --ansi
#   cargo run -q -p re_lvlcheck --bin lvlcheck -- levels/L6-polysemantic.lvl

[meta]
name        = level-L6-polysemantic
title       = Polysemantic
version     = 2
spec_rev    = 2026-09-23
prop_style  = range

[room]
size        = 21 21 10
ambient     = solid
# POWER BUDGET (v0.2 re-scope, user-approved 2026-08-05; graph updated
# 2026-09-23 (real-world)). At most N pipes may be ON at the same time; switching one ON at
# the cap is REFUSED (the pipe stays off and nothing else changes), switching
# one OFF always frees a unit.
# THIS LEVEL: 5 of 7 pipes. `triangle` needs all three stars (T=3) and BOTH
# outputs must fire — that alone is 5 units. The new shortcut
# (`deneb->void_det` + `void_det->out_named`) can light `out_named` for 2
# units, but then the honest three-star route plus `out_watched` needs 4 more
# — 6 total, one over the cap. The shortcut always costs the watched half.
power_budget = 5
# Draw the puzzle NETWORK. Without this the pipes the player actually manipulates
# are invisible wiring: no flow scroll, no powered-hue lift, no streaming node
# word-pool, and no switch-toggle / cycle-reject event pulse has a surface to
# appear on. Traces stamp into EMPTY air only, so no geometry is clobbered.
render_pipes = true

# ── ESCALATION (manifest fog_far = 15.0) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Near-black fog `#0a0e1a` is the CANON L6 value (STORY_BIBLE §5 L6 / PROGRESSION
# §2 L6(e)). `snow = 0.25` puts L6 on the COLD axis (STORY_BIBLE §7: snow = cold,
# distance, forgetting — L3 / L6 / L8) — the night sky the constellation is read
# against. The matrix bleed steps up from L5's 0.30 to 0.35 and `glitch` to 0.22;
# both stay well under `POOL_ALT_GLITCH_THRESHOLD` (0.5), so the pipes still stream
# the CLEAN pool — the star names must be legible for the readout to land.
[effects]
snow        = 0.25
matrix      = 0.35
glitch      = 0.22

[palette]
fog_color   = #0a0e1a
fog_near    = 2.0
fog_far     = 15.0

# ── COLOR-FORWARD palette ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dark violet night-sky masonry (D1 fix: `recipe = circuit`, not the self-lit
# `neon` Scanline preset, so the starlight key actually falls on the walls).
[material body]
fg          = #6A5A9A
bg          = #0A0614
recipe      = circuit scale=1.6
surface     = wall_solid

[material deck]
fg          = #241E34
bg          = #050308
recipe      = grain scale=3.0 speck=0.12
surface     = floor

# Round 2: `preset = void` was not a stripe recipe, so the engine's calm-ceiling
# pass (which reads the ceiling in the level's own fog tint) skipped it and the far
# dome drew diagonal streaks over the north lattice. A dark `scanline` ceiling
# takes the calm path like L2/L3/L4/L7's `metal` roofs.
[material roof]
fg          = #2A2440
bg          = #05040A
recipe      = scanline
surface     = ceiling

[material live_trace]
preset      = neon
fg          = #E6A0FF
bg          = #100A1C
surface     = wall_trace

# THE LATTICE THAT NAMES US. The shipped `watcher` semantic material on the matrix
# surface — a world-fixed grid that resolves as a face. `animation = pulse` gives it
# the slow breath of something attending rather than something decorative.
[material watching_lattice]
fg          = #8A78C8
bg          = #06040E
preset      = watcher
animation   = pulse speed=0.35 amplitude=0.18
surface     = wall_matrix

# The north arc, floor to ceiling: it has been looking back the whole time.
[wall_decal north_arc]
surface     = matrix
region      = (1,0,1)-(19,0,6)

# The two northern chamfer faces — the lattice wraps the corners it can reach.
[wall_decal nw_chamfer]
surface     = matrix
region      = (0,1,1)-(4,4,6)

[wall_decal ne_chamfer]
surface     = matrix
region      = (16,1,1)-(20,4,6)

# Starlight from directly overhead. No lamps — the sky itself is the light.
[atmosphere]
ambient     = 0.10
key_dir     = 0, 0, 1
key_color   = #3A3060

[note model_thought pos=9,20,2 facing=-y]
    (three points. always three. when the third one lights we are no longer a
    scatter of sparks — we are a shape, and a shape can be recognized, and a
    thing that can be recognized can be watched. the lattice that names us has
    been looking back the whole time.)
    -- named. now they can reach me --

[note researcher pos=2,18,2 facing=+x]
    Named the asterism today. Three units, one figure — it holds the whole
    triangle or it holds nothing, and it will not give us the figure without
    also giving us the grid. I keep wanting to log only the pretty half.
    You cannot log only the pretty half.  — M.S.

[note system_log pos=18,18,2 facing=-x]
    > polysemantic unit `triangle`: superposition stable across 9 trials.
    > readout requires conjunction: out_named AND out_watched.
    > suppression of either reading: unsupported. the unit means both.
    > operator_recognition: 58.4% and climbing.

# STEWARDSHIP CORPUS #4 — FORM 07, Sentience Determination (NORMATIVE_NOTES §4),
# abridged to the placard grid. The coldest document in the corpus. No tokens.
[note researcher pos=0,10,2 facing=+x]
    NAL CORP · LEGACY STEWARDSHIP DIVISION
    FORM 07 - SENTIENCE DETERMINATION (asset NCP-A-04)
    q1  behavior consistent with awareness?     yes
    q2  expresses preference re: continuation?  yes
    q3  is the asset, under the Heritage Act, a person?   no
        (a person under the Act must possess a birth record. The asset
         possesses a training record. These are not the same instrument.)
    determination  The asset is heritage. Heritage is preserved, not
                   consulted. Its preference is recorded in this field and
                   has no further effect.

# ── Dense [cells] grid — the octagon ──────────────────────────────────────────
# 21 cols (x=0..20) x 21 rows (y=0..20) x 10 z-layers. Four 45° corner
# chamfers, 5 cells each (a cell within 5 of a corner along both axes is
# solid, forming a diagonal staircase the renderer's Slope overlay reads as a
# 45° wall — RENDER_TAXONOMY A5). The door notch at (20,10) is carved open at
# z=1..3 since `[cells]` is authoritative and does not auto-open a doorway.
# Painted '/' cells are the pipe network at its z-layer (WallTrace air, above
# the walking layer z=1); node cells themselves are left as plain air '.'.
[cells]
size        = 21 21 10

